      "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0f1c0c91-01d2-5448-913d-0fa0508df9b8",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/71/7195a8606bfb19179b3d66daead30ff749c4d8381ed3bb068f214469058497d2.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "14c1f897-d524-5a2b-b496-fa5e337dc9be",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "ae4ac95b-88c1-56fd-b605-82f0d561d688",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{4x}{9y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "53dc0be3-ad46-5179-bfe8-d271a27ab4c0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{2x}{3y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e8948326-dffb-56bd-8493-c8b123212c66",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{9x}{4y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "76e00056-a562-5556-9114-d8a8370cc1b8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{9y}{4x}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "42db9b1e-39a8-5937-a0b9-625f47db7fbf",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{4x}{9y}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "ae4ac95b-88c1-56fd-b605-82f0d561d688"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $3$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{9}+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    "generation": {
