    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a0940c9c-6087-560d-be99-668d9382e6a8",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/ae/aeb820de54dc7302bb833ce41db2ae0ff5bdd8c3ddfd90528fc55bc8ae1b3a51.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "c1c1a89c-fe68-5c9c-894e-5ac854573ab9",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "b00745fa-c8cc-518e-a96a-16c82a0b06c0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{y}{25x}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "40cb79cf-738f-5a07-9083-585b4b752d17",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{25x}{y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8e281887-436b-5c70-a6fc-e2ad8a239d44",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{25x}{y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5265da00-f084-5cc0-a730-b674ea37e66b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{5x}{y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "23c303d4-cdc8-5588-b871-2d1cb2b186cc",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{x}{25y}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "8e281887-436b-5c70-a6fc-e2ad8a239d44"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $5,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1\\,\u27f9\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}\\right) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{25x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
